# Z numerals as first-class symbolic leaves, plus the N -> Z promotion
# that COMPLETES natural partiality: subtraction results and negations
# that do not exist over the naturals become zint terms.
#
# PREREQUISITES (import order):
#   .import arithmetic          # or binary-arithmetic / binary-nand-arithmetic
#   .import integer-arithmetic  # incl. the uniform operator facade
#   .import symbolic-core
#   .import symbolic-minus
#   .import symbolic-integers
#
# NUMERIC FOLDING over Z needs no rules here at all: a red form over two
# zint leaves IS an ordinary +/-/* fact, the facade routes it to
# z+/z-/zx and re-exposes the result under =, and symbolic-core's SN
# bridge adopts it -- the exact mechanism of natural constant folding.
# This module only contributes what the facade cannot: leaf status,
# neutral/absorbing identities against SYMBOLIC operands, negation of
# numerals, and the N -> Z promotions.
#
# MIXED WORLDS: the naturals' identity rules (X + &0, X * &1, ...) and
# the zint rules below coexist -- different zero/one nodes for different
# number worlds. This is what lets diff.zph's natural &0/&1 seeds work
# unchanged over Z coefficients: d((neg zint &3) * x)/dx assembles
# ((&0 * x) + ((neg zint &3) * &1)), and the NATURAL identities reduce
# it to (neg zint &3).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rule ZL1 -- zint leaves are their own normal forms (the SB pattern;
# without this base case, parents of zint children would never reduce)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
((G zint N) needssimp (G zint N)) => ((G zint N) simp (G zint N))

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rules ZSR -- neutral and absorbing elements over Z numerals, both
# orientations (mirroring symbolic-core's SR block). Conflict-free with
# the facade fold on every all-numeral overlap: z+/zx results of
# canonical operands are canonical, so both paths yield the same node.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(T red (X + (pos zint &0))) => (T rw X)
(T red ((pos zint &0) + X)) => (T rw X)
(T red (X - (pos zint &0))) => (T rw X)
(T red (X * (pos zint &1))) => (T rw X)
(T red ((pos zint &1) * X)) => (T rw X)
(T red (X * (pos zint &0))) => (T rw (pos zint &0))
(T red ((pos zint &0) * X)) => (T rw (pos zint &0))

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rules ZN -- negation of Z numerals. The nonzero case is guarded via an
# in-system comparison so that (neg zint &0) is never produced and rw
# stays single-valued (the zero case has its own direct rule).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(T red (neg of (pos zint A))) => (A cmp &0)
(T red (neg of (pos zint A)), A > &0) => (T rw (neg zint A))
(T red (neg of (pos zint &0))) => (T rw (pos zint &0))
(T red (neg of (neg zint A))) => (T rw (pos zint A))

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rules ZP -- N -> Z promotion: complete natural partiality.
#
# Negation of a natural numeral has no natural value; here it becomes a
# zint. The zero case overlaps with symbolic-minus's (neg of &0) rule --
# deliberately conflict-free, both yield the natural &0.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(T red (neg of (A cons R))) => ((A cons R) cmp &0)
(T red (neg of (A cons R)), (A cons R) > &0) => (T rw (neg zint (A cons R)))
(T red (neg of (A cons R)), (A cons R) == &0) => (T rw &0)

# Natural subtraction with minuend < subtrahend derives no natural
# result (partiality by absence) -- so the SN fold is silent exactly
# where these rules fire, and vice versa: single-valuedness by case
# disjointness. The reversed subtraction is asserted as an ordinary -
# fact for the natural module to answer (MA1/MA2 cascade).
(T red ((A cons R) - (B cons S))) => ((A cons R) cmp (B cons S))
(T red ((A cons R) - (B cons S)), (A cons R) < (B cons S))
=> ((B cons S) - (A cons R))
(T red ((A cons R) - (B cons S)), (A cons R) < (B cons S),
 ((B cons S) - (A cons R)) = D)
=> (T rw (neg zint D))
